== Organization and governance ==

=== Governor ===

The AISB is headed by a [[Governor of the Adonian International Settlement Bank|Governor]], who is appointed by the [[Adonian Assembly]] for a renewable five-year term. The Governor serves as the chief executive of the institution, responsible for day-to-day management, representing the AISB in international forums, and chairing the Board of Directors. The Governor may not simultaneously serve as the governor or head of any member state central bank or national government.

=== Board of Directors ===

The [[Board of Directors of the Adonian International Settlement Bank|Board of Directors]] consists of the central bank governors of all AISB member states, or their designated representatives. The Board meets at least twice annually to set policy, approve settlement procedures, oversee the institution's operations, and admit new members. The [[Governor of the Adonian Monetary Authority]] sits as an ex officio member of the Board to facilitate coordination between the two institutions.

Each member state has one vote on the Board. Decisions on operational matters require a simple majority, while changes to settlement procedures, amendments to the AISB charter, and the admission of new members require a two-thirds majority.

=== Committees ===

The Board delegates day-to-day policy matters to standing committees, which include the Monetary Policy Coordination Committee, the Settlement Operations Committee, the Financial Stability Committee, and the Audit and Risk Committee. Committee memberships are drawn from the Board and chaired by a Board member elected by their peers.

== Functions ==

=== Settlement services ===

The AISB's primary function is to facilitate the settlement of payments between the central banks of AC member states. The institution operates the [[Adonian Settlement System]], a {{w|real-time gross settlement}} platform that processes transactions in both [[International dollar]]s and member state national currencies. Central banks maintain accounts with the AISB, through which they settle cross-border payments, currency swaps, and other inter-state financial transactions.

The Adonian Settlement System processes an average of [TBD] transactions per day, with a daily settlement value of approximately [TBD] billion International dollars. The system operates continuously across AC time zones, with settlement windows aligned to the business hours of member state financial markets.

=== Banking services to AC institutions ===

The AISB provides banking services to the institutions of the Adonian Community, including the [[Adonian Assembly]], the [[Adonian Secretariat]], the [[Adonian Court of Justice]], and other AC bodies. These services include account management, payment processing, foreign exchange transactions, and short-term financing. The AISB also serves as the depositary for AC trust funds and special accounts established by the Adonian Assembly.

=== Financial stability monitoring ===

The AISB monitors financial stability across AC member states, collecting and analyzing data on banking systems, capital flows, and exchange rate movements. The institution publishes the annual ''Report on Financial Stability in the Adonian Community'', which assesses systemic risks and vulnerabilities in the AC financial system. The AISB also provides confidential policy recommendations to member state central banks and contributes to the financial stability work of the [[Adonian Economic Council]].

=== Research and statistics ===

The AISB conducts research on monetary economics, international finance, and banking supervision through its research department. The institution publishes working papers, statistical reports, and periodical publications, including the ''AISB Quarterly Review'' and the ''Statistical Bulletin of the Adonian Community''. The AISB also maintains comprehensive databases on international banking statistics, exchange rates, and financial market indicators, which are made available to member central banks and the public.

=== Emergency lending ===

The AISB provides emergency lending facilities to member state central banks facing {{w|liquidity}} shortages. These facilities are intended to address temporary {{w|balance of payments}} difficulties and are subject to conditions set by the Board of Directors. Emergency lending requires a two-thirds majority approval by the Board and is typically extended in coordination with the [[Adonian Monetary Authority]] and the [[Adonian Economic Council]].

== Relationship with other AC institutions ==

The AISB and the [[Adonian Monetary Authority]] are the two principal financial institutions of the Adonian Community. The AMA is responsible for issuing the [[International dollar]], setting monetary policy, and managing the energy standard. The AISB handles the operational settlement of payments between central banks and AC institutions. The two institutions maintain close cooperation through the ex officio membership of the AMA Governor on the AISB Board of Directors and through joint committees on monetary policy coordination and financial stability.

The AISB also works with the [[Adonian Economic Council]] on matters related to financial regulation, economic surveillance, and the coordination of economic policies among member states. The AISB provides the Council with statistical data, financial stability assessments, and technical analysis to support its policy recommendations.

== Member central banks ==

All AC member state central banks are eligible for membership in the AISB. As of 2026, the AISB has [TBD] member central banks. Member central banks maintain settlement accounts with the AISB and participate in the Adonian Settlement System.

